+# Rekor Restore Drill + TLS Lifecycle Playbook
+
+Objectives:
+- Validate reconstrucion from backups and test TLS cert rotation for Rekor endpoints.
+
+Prereqs:
+- S3 backup bucket and access credentials.
+- Staging RDS and Rekor staging deployment.
+- Certificate authority access (internal PKI or public CA).
+
+Restore drill:
+1. Identify latest backup: `aws s3 ls s3://aegis-rekor-backups/`
+2. Download and restore: `pg_restore -h ${STAGING_DB_HOST} -U ${STAGING_DB_USER} -d rekor /tmp/rekor.dump`
+3. Update Rekor deployment to staging DB and restart.
+4. Validate API: `/api/v1/log/log_info` and sample entry reads.
+
+TLS lifecycle:
+1. Generate new cert (via internal CA) or use cert-manager to issue a new cert.
+2. Create k8s TLS secret: `kubectl -n rekor create secret tls rekor-tls --cert=rekor.crt --key=rekor.key --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl apply -f -`
+3. Roll cert by updating secret and performing rolling restart of rekor deployment.
+4. Verify Rekor clients accept new cert and re-check Rekor proofs.
+
+Validation:
+- Use `rekor verify` client or `curl --cacert` to validate TLS handshake and log entries.
+
